SLURM
setupmjr hpc slurm
This installs SLURM helpers into ~/.local/bin, including:

slurm-sbatch for job submission and submission records;
slurm-sintx for interactive sessions;
slurm-squeue for listing the current user’s jobs.

Release assets
GitHub Releases publish Linux, macOS and Windows binaries for amd64 and arm64. Archives are .tar.gz on Linux/macOS and .zip on Windows. Installer scripts use the stable bare-binary names:
setupmjr_linux_&lt;arch&gt;
setupmjr_darwin_&lt;arch&gt;
setupmjr_windows_&lt;arch&gt;.exe

Protected-token fallback
When no persistent gh login is available, setupmjr reuses the first available credential from:

GH_TOKEN;
GITHUB_TOKEN;
~/.config/setupmjr/auth/github.token;
a token entered at the prompt.

The auth directory is mode 0700 and github.token is mode 0600 on POSIX systems. Git is configured with a host-specific credential helper that reads this file when Git requests a credential; the literal token is not written into Git configuration or shell startup files.
For tools that consume GH_TOKEN, setupmjr places a non-secret managed block in Bash and Zsh login.sh files. The block reads the protected token file when the shell starts.
setupmjr git auth text explicitly selects this fallback. The text name remains for backwards compatibility.
